1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,021
Shipping to the edge fails on the basics:

2
00:00:03,021 --> 00:00:10,514
images pinned to latest, no resource limits, no health probes, containers running as root, secrets in config files.

3
00:00:10,514 --> 00:00:17,290
On constrained nodes, each one means unpredictable behavior, and developers lose hours digging for them.

4
00:00:18,090 --> 00:00:23,223
Hyperion Sentinel turns that into one conversation inside the HYPER-AI IDE:

5
00:00:23,223 --> 00:00:32,190
it inspects your real workspace, explains with evidence, fixes what's safe, asks before anything risky, and proves the improvement.

6
00:00:32,990 --> 00:00:33,918
How it works:

7
00:00:33,918 --> 00:00:41,982
deterministic analyzers produce the facts, across Docker, Kubernetes, Compose, and HYPER-AI application profiles.

8
00:00:41,982 --> 00:00:44,408
The language model only converses.

9
00:00:44,408 --> 00:00:48,690
Every change is an IDE action you confirm, then re-verified.

10
00:00:51,606 --> 00:00:55,178
Now live, in the real IDE, with the real Llama model.

11
00:00:55,178 --> 00:00:58,414
I ask Hyperion to prepare this app for the edge.

12
00:00:58,414 --> 00:01:06,436
It reports an Edge Readiness score of thirty-five out of a hundred, every finding tied to a file, a line, and evidence.

13
00:01:06,517 --> 00:01:07,976
What should I fix first?

14
00:01:07,976 --> 00:01:10,227
It ranks by impact, and explains why.

15
00:01:13,395 --> 00:01:15,594
Fix everything you safely can.

16
00:01:15,594 --> 00:01:16,107
A plan:

17
00:01:16,107 --> 00:01:22,045
safe changes, changes needing my confirmation, and manual items it never touches.

18
00:01:22,045 --> 00:01:23,805
Nothing has changed yet.

19
00:01:24,306 --> 00:01:25,042
I confirm.

20
00:01:25,042 --> 00:01:32,993
Files are rewritten by IDE actions, the deployment opens in the editor, and Hyperion re-reads the workspace:

21
00:01:32,993 --> 00:01:35,276
thirty-five becomes sixty-five.

22
00:01:36,354 --> 00:01:41,214
It answers HYPER-AI questions from the official documentation, with sources.

23
00:01:45,460 --> 00:01:48,920
Off-topic requests are refused, and no files are touched.

24
00:01:51,405 --> 00:01:53,775
And destructive actions always ask first.

25
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:00,930
Hyperion Sentinel:

26
00:02:00,930 --> 00:02:03,582
inspect, explain, fix safely, verify.

27
00:02:03,582 --> 00:02:07,093
Open source on GitHub, shipped as a Docker image.

28
00:02:07,093 --> 00:02:07,810
Thank you.
